/-!
# The two per-slice inputs of [Stacks, Tag 0A0E] over an affine open, at an arbitrary ideal

Let `Y` be a locally Noetherian scheme, not assumed quasi-compact, and let `ℐ ⊂ 𝒪_Y` be an
arbitrary quasi-coherent sheaf of ideals. The Koszul approach to part (1) of [Stacks, Tag 0A0K]
in `KoszulAdicQuotientSite.lean` needs two things of the site it runs on: that the ideal sheaf be
generated by finitely many *global* sections, and that the Koszul cohomology sheaves be pro-zero
below the top degree. Neither holds on `Y` itself: the pro-vanishing is false at `r = 1`,
`f = x`, `ℱ = 𝒪` on `⊔ᵢ Spec k[x]/(xⁱ)`, where the level needed to kill `H⁰` on the `i`-th chart
is `n + i`, so that no single level works for all charts. This file supplies both on the slice
over an affine open, and assembles them into part (1) on that slice.

## Main results

* `Stacks.KoszulProZero.exists_eq_generatedIdealSheaf_overIdeal_affine`: `ℐ|_U` is the ideal
  sheaf generated by finitely many global sections of `𝒪_U`. The generators are sections over `U`
  and need not extend to global sections of `𝒪_Y`.
* `Stacks.KoszulProZero.exists_koszulDualSystemOn_over_homologyMap_eq_zero_of_section`: the
  pro-vanishing on that slice for such a family, with no compactness hypothesis.
* `Stacks.KoszulProZero.isDerivedLimit_adicReductionTower_completion_over_of_section`: part (1)
  on the slice at the ideal sheaf generated by finitely many sections over the affine open.
* `Stacks.KoszulProZero.exists_isDerivedLimit_adicReductionTower_completion_overIdeal_affine`:
  part (1) on the slice at an arbitrary quasi-coherent sheaf of ideals.

## Implementation notes

`KoszulDualProZeroSlice.lean` proves the pro-vanishing on the slice over an affine open for a
family obtained by restricting global sections of `𝒪_Y` along
`AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.globalSectionOver`. The generators an arbitrary quasi-coherent
ideal sheaf supplies over an affine open are sections of `Γ(Y, U)` and in general extend to no
global section, so that statement does not apply to them. The proof here is the same model
argument at the single model `A = Γ(Y, U)`, `M = Γ(ℱ, U)` over the basis of basic opens of `U`;
only the step identifying the generators' values over a basic open changes, and for a section of
`Γ(Y, U)` it is `globalSectionVal_globalSectionOfSection` rather than `globalSectionVal_map`.

Part (1) is obtained on the slice `(𝒞/U, 𝒪_U)` by instantiating
`AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.isDerivedLimit_adicReductionTower_completion`: the slice of a
`RingedSite.{u, u, u}` is again one, `HasDerivedCategory.standard` gives its derived category, and
the `HasCoproduct`/`HasProduct` binders of that theorem are found by instance search.

These per-slice statements do not globalize directly:
`CategoryTheory.Pretriangulated.IsDerivedLimit` is the existence of a distinguished triangle over
the product in `D(𝒪)` and carries no comparison map, so it is not a property that can be checked
on a cover.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 01P7](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01P7)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0A0E](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0A0E)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0A0K](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0A0K)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open AlgebraicGeometry CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits Opposite

universe u

namespace Stacks.KoszulProZero

section AffineSlice

variable (Y : Scheme.{u}) [IsLocallyNoetherian Y] {r : ℕ}
  (ℱ : Y.Modules) [ℱ.IsCoherent] (U : Y.affineOpens) (g : Fin r → Γ(Y, U.1))

omit [IsLocallyNoetherian Y] in
/-- The value over a basic open of the slice-global section attached to a section over the
affine open is the restriction of that section. -/
theorem basicOpenRestrict_eq_globalSectionVal_globalSectionOfSection
    (h : Γ(Y, U.1)) (a : Γ(Y, U.1)) :
    basicOpenRestrict Y U.1 h a =
      _root_.AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.globalSectionVal
        (_root_.AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.globalSectionOfSection
          (_root_.Stacks.SheafOfModules.opensRingedSite Y.sheaf) U.1 a)
        (op (Over.mk (homOfLE (Y.basicOpen_le h)))) := by
  refine Eq.trans ?_
    (_root_.AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.globalSectionVal_globalSectionOfSection
      (_root_.Stacks.SheafOfModules.opensRingedSite Y.sheaf) U.1 a
      (op (Over.mk (homOfLE (Y.basicOpen_le h))))).symm
  rfl

/-- **The cohomology sheaves of the tower of [Stacks, Tag 0A0E] are pro-zero below the top
degree on the slice over an affine open, for a family of generators that are sections over that
affine open.**

Let `Y` be a locally Noetherian scheme — *not* assumed quasi-compact — let `ℱ` be a coherent
`𝒪_Y`-module, let `U` be an affine open and let `g_1, …, g_r ∈ Γ(Y, U)`. On the localization of
the opens ringed site of `Y` at `U`, where each `g_i` is a *global* section of `𝒪_U` by
`AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.globalSectionOfSection`, every level `n` and every degree `p`
below the top degree `r` admit a later level `m` at which the transition of 0A0E's tower induces
the zero map on the degree-`p` cohomology sheaf.

This is the form the generators of an arbitrary quasi-coherent sheaf of ideals come in:
`Stacks.KoszulProZero.exists_eq_generatedIdealSheaf_overIdeal_affine` produces sections of
`Γ(Y, U)`, which in general extend to no global section of `𝒪_Y`, so
`Stacks.KoszulProZero.exists_koszulDualSystemOn_over_homologyMap_eq_zero` — stated for a family
restricted from global sections — does not apply to them.

The proof is `Stacks.KoszulProZero.exists_koszulDualSystemOn_homologyMap_eq_zero_of_model` at the
single model `A = Γ(Y, U)`, `a_i = g_i`, `M = Γ(ℱ, U)`: the basic opens of `U` are a basis of the
slice site, over each of them `Γ(𝒪_Y, Y.basicOpen h)` is a localization of `A` hence flat and
`Γ(ℱ, Y.basicOpen h)` is the base change of `M`, and the Artin–Rees level is computed once over
the model. No maximum over a cover is taken, which is why no quasi-compactness of `Y` appears —
and must not: the pro-vanishing is false on `⊔ᵢ Spec k[x]/(xⁱ)`, where chart `i` needs
Artin–Rees level `≥ n + i`. -/
@[sga "2 II Lemma11" "special case"]
theorem exists_koszulDualSystemOn_over_homologyMap_eq_zero_of_section (n : ℕ) (p : ℤ)
    (hp : p < r) :
    ∃ (m : ℕ) (hnm : n ≤ m), HomologicalComplex.homologyMap
      ((_root_.AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.koszulDualSystemOn
          ((_root_.Stacks.SheafOfModules.opensRingedSite Y.sheaf).over U.1)
          (fun i => _root_.AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.globalSectionOfSection
            (_root_.Stacks.SheafOfModules.opensRingedSite Y.sheaf) U.1 (g i))
          ((SheafOfModules.overFunctor.{u} ((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf
              (_root_.Stacks.SheafOfModules.opensRingedSite Y.sheaf).O)) U.1).obj
            (show SheafOfModules.{u} ((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf
                (_root_.Stacks.SheafOfModules.opensRingedSite Y.sheaf).O)) from ℱ))).map
        (homOfLE hnm).op) p = 0 := by
  obtain ⟨hqc, hft⟩ :=
    Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.CoherentTFAE.isQuasicoherent_isFiniteType_of_isCoherent ℱ
  have := hqc
  have := IsLocallyNoetherian.component_noetherian U
  have : Module.Finite Γ(Y, U.1) Γ(ℱ, U.1) :=
    AlgebraicGeometry.moduleFinite_sections_on_affine ℱ U.1 U.2
  refine exists_koszulDualSystemOn_homologyMap_eq_zero_of_model
    ((_root_.Stacks.SheafOfModules.opensRingedSite Y.sheaf).over U.1) _ _
    Γ(Y, U.1) g (ModuleCat.of Γ(Y, U.1) Γ(ℱ, U.1)) (fun W => ?_) n p hp
  refine ⟨fun Z _ => ∃ h : Γ(Y, U.1), Z = Over.mk (homOfLE (Y.basicOpen_le h)), ?_, ?_⟩
  · intro x hx
    obtain ⟨h, hgle, hxg⟩ :=
      U.2.exists_basicOpen_le (V := W.unop.left) ⟨x, hx⟩ (leOfHom W.unop.hom hx)
    refine ⟨Y.basicOpen h, homOfLE hgle, ?_, hxg⟩
    rw [Sieve.overEquiv_iff]
    exact ⟨_, 𝟙 _, Over.homMk (homOfLE hgle), ⟨h, rfl⟩, by simp⟩
  · rintro Z i ⟨h, rfl⟩
    refine ⟨basicOpenRestrict Y U.1 h, ModuleCat.of Γ(Y, U.1) Γ(Y, Y.basicOpen h),
      fun j => ?_, flat_sections_basicOpen Y U h, ⟨basicOpenModelIso Y ℱ U h⟩⟩
    exact basicOpenRestrict_eq_globalSectionVal_globalSectionOfSection Y U h (g j)

end AffineSlice

section AffineSliceIdeal

open AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite

variable (Y : Scheme.{u}) [IsLocallyNoetherian Y] (ideal : Y.IdealSheafData)
  (U : Y.affineOpens)

/-- **At an affine open of a locally Noetherian scheme an arbitrary quasi-coherent sheaf of
ideals is, on the slice, the ideal sheaf generated by finitely many global sections**, in the
spelling `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.generatedIdealSheaf` that the Koszul chain of
`KoszulAdicQuotientSite.lean` is stated with.

`Stacks.Algebraization.exists_eq_idealOfGlobalSections_overIdeal_affine` gives the same
identification in the spelling `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.idealOfGlobalSections`, and
`AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.generatedIdealSheaf_eq_idealOfGlobalSections` says the two
constructions agree. The generators are sections over `U` and need not extend to global sections
of the structure sheaf; on the slice they are global, which is the whole point of passing to
it. -/
theorem exists_eq_generatedIdealSheaf_overIdeal_affine :
    ∃ (r : ℕ) (g : Fin r → Γ(Y, U.1)),
      _root_.AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.overIdeal
          (_root_.Stacks.Algebraization.idealSheafSiteSubmodule ideal) U.1 =
        _root_.AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.generatedIdealSheaf
          (fun i => _root_.AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.globalSectionOfSection
            (_root_.Stacks.SheafOfModules.opensRingedSite Y.sheaf) U.1 (g i)) := by
  obtain ⟨r, g, _, _, hgen⟩ :=
    _root_.Stacks.Algebraization.exists_eq_idealOfGlobalSections_overIdeal_affine ideal U
  exact ⟨r, g, hgen.trans
    (_root_.AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.generatedIdealSheaf_eq_idealOfGlobalSections _).symm⟩

end AffineSliceIdeal


section AffineSlicePartOne

/- The priority on `HasDerivedCategory.standard` is needed: with a plain local instance, another
`HasDerivedCategory` instance from the import closure of `LocalCalculationFiniteType.lean` is
tried first and the additivity of the shift functors of `D(𝒪_U)` is not found when elaborating the
`CategoryTheory.Pretriangulated.IsDerivedLimit` conclusions below. The value `100000` is the one
`LocalCalculationFiniteType.lean` uses. -/
attribute [local instance 100000] HasDerivedCategory.standard
attribute [local instance] AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.hasSheafCompose_forget₂_ringCat
attribute [local instance] Stacks.Cohomology.SiteModules.site_hasSheafify_addCommGrp
attribute [local instance] Stacks.Cohomology.SiteModules.site_wEqualsLocallyBijective_addCommGrp

variable (Y : Scheme.{u}) [IsLocallyNoetherian Y] {r : ℕ} (U : Y.Opens)
  (g : Fin r → Γ(Y, U))

/-- **Part (1) of [Stacks, Tag 0A0K] on the slice over an affine open of a locally Noetherian
scheme, at the ideal sheaf generated by finitely many sections over that open** — with no
quasi-compactness of `Y` and no global generating family. For an **arbitrary** object `K` of
`D(𝒪_U)` the Čech completion of `K` along that ideal sheaf is a derived limit of the tower
`n ↦ K ⊗^𝐋_{𝒪_U} 𝒪_U/ℐⁿ⁺¹`.

This is `AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.isDerivedLimit_adicReductionTower_completion` — part (1) on
an arbitrary ringed site, whose only hypothesis is the pro-vanishing of the Koszul cohomology
sheaves below the top degree — instantiated at the slice `(𝒞/U, 𝒪_U)` of the opens site of `Y`,
with that pro-vanishing discharged by
`Stacks.KoszulProZero.exists_koszulDualSystemOn_over_homologyMap_eq_zero_of_section` at the
structure sheaf, coherent because `Y` is locally Noetherian. -/
theorem isDerivedLimit_adicReductionTower_completion_over_of_section
    (hU : _root_.AlgebraicGeometry.IsAffineOpen U)
    (K : DerivedCategory (SheafOfModules.{u}
      ((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf
        ((_root_.Stacks.SheafOfModules.opensRingedSite Y.sheaf).over U).O)))) :
    CategoryTheory.Pretriangulated.IsDerivedLimit
      (_root_.AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.adicReductionTower
        ((_root_.Stacks.SheafOfModules.opensRingedSite Y.sheaf).over U)
        (_root_.AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.generatedIdealSheaf
          (fun i => _root_.AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.globalSectionOfSection
            (_root_.Stacks.SheafOfModules.opensRingedSite Y.sheaf) U (g i))) K)
      ((_root_.AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.completionFunctor
        ((_root_.Stacks.SheafOfModules.opensRingedSite Y.sheaf).over U)
        (fun i => _root_.AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.globalSectionOfSection
          (_root_.Stacks.SheafOfModules.opensRingedSite Y.sheaf) U (g i))).obj K) := by
  have hco : _root_.SheafOfModules.IsCoherent
      (show Y.Modules from _root_.SheafOfModules.unit
        ((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf
          (_root_.Stacks.SheafOfModules.opensRingedSite Y.sheaf).O))) :=
    Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.CoherentTFAE.isCoherent_unit Y
  exact _root_.AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.isDerivedLimit_adicReductionTower_completion
    _ _ K fun n p hp =>
      exists_koszulDualSystemOn_over_homologyMap_eq_zero_of_section Y
        (show Y.Modules from _root_.SheafOfModules.unit
          ((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf
            (_root_.Stacks.SheafOfModules.opensRingedSite Y.sheaf).O))) ⟨U, hU⟩ g n p hp

/-- **Part (1) of [Stacks, Tag 0A0K] on the slice over an affine open of a locally Noetherian
scheme, at an ARBITRARY quasi-coherent sheaf of ideals** — no quasi-compactness of `Y`, no global
generating family, and nothing asked of the object `K`.

The restriction of `ℐ` to the slice is the ideal sheaf generated by finitely many sections over
the affine open (`Stacks.KoszulProZero.exists_eq_generatedIdealSheaf_overIdeal_affine`), and at
such a family part (1) is
`Stacks.KoszulProZero.isDerivedLimit_adicReductionTower_completion_over_of_section`. The
generators are returned because the Čech completion
`AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.completionFunctor` is indexed by them; the tower, by contrast, is
stated at the restricted ideal itself. -/
theorem exists_isDerivedLimit_adicReductionTower_completion_overIdeal_affine
    (ideal : Y.IdealSheafData) (V : Y.affineOpens) :
    ∃ (r : ℕ) (g : Fin r → Γ(Y, V.1)),
      _root_.AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.overIdeal
          (_root_.Stacks.Algebraization.idealSheafSiteSubmodule ideal) V.1 =
        _root_.AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.generatedIdealSheaf
          (fun i => _root_.AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.globalSectionOfSection
            (_root_.Stacks.SheafOfModules.opensRingedSite Y.sheaf) V.1 (g i)) ∧
      ∀ K : DerivedCategory (SheafOfModules.{u}
        ((Stacks.SheafOfModules.Tensor.ringSheaf
          ((_root_.Stacks.SheafOfModules.opensRingedSite Y.sheaf).over V.1).O))),
        CategoryTheory.Pretriangulated.IsDerivedLimit
          (_root_.AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.adicReductionTower
            ((_root_.Stacks.SheafOfModules.opensRingedSite Y.sheaf).over V.1)
            (_root_.AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.overIdeal
              (_root_.Stacks.Algebraization.idealSheafSiteSubmodule ideal) V.1) K)
          ((_root_.AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.completionFunctor
            ((_root_.Stacks.SheafOfModules.opensRingedSite Y.sheaf).over V.1)
            (fun i => _root_.AlgebraicGeometry.RingedSite.globalSectionOfSection
              (_root_.Stacks.SheafOfModules.opensRingedSite Y.sheaf) V.1 (g i))).obj K) := by
  obtain ⟨r, g, hgen⟩ := exists_eq_generatedIdealSheaf_overIdeal_affine Y ideal V
  refine ⟨r, g, hgen, fun K => ?_⟩
  rw [hgen]
  exact isDerivedLimit_adicReductionTower_completion_over_of_section Y V.1 g V.2 K

end AffineSlicePartOne


end Stacks.KoszulProZero

end
